ultant<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Compliance, Information Security and Data Analyst<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Risk Management and Business Intelligence Strategist<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6b0ec11 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"6b0ec11\" data-element_type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Program Overview A Bachelor\u2019s degree in Risk Management and Business Intelligence is a program that provides students with a comprehensive understanding of the intersection between business analytics, information technology, and risk management. The study combines theoretical concepts with practical applications in order to prepare students to analyse data and make informed decisions that mitigate business risks and improve organizational performance. Students learn to develop risk management strategies, assess potential threats to businesses, evaluate financial risks, and analyse market trends. They also gain skills in data mining, statistical analysis, decision-making, database management, and software development. The program covers topics such as business intelligence, strategic management, enterprise risk management, fraud detection and prevention, cyber security, and compliance. Graduates can pursue careers in various industries, including finance, insurance, healthcare, government, and consulting firms. Overall, a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Risk Management and Business Intelligence provides students with a strong foundation in both technical and business skills, making them well-equipped to succeed in today\u2019s data-driven business world. Program Learning Outcomes At the end of the 4-year program, graduates will be able to: Use quantitative and qualitative tools to assess risk and identify potential threats to businesses and organizations. Develop and implement comprehensive risk management plans to minimize losses and protect the interests of their companies and clients. Apply critical thinking and analytical skills to business intelligence data and use it to recommend data-driven strategies to help organizations remain competitive. Demonstrate knowledge of information security principles to protect data privacy and prevent data breaches. Effectively communicate complex risk management, business intelligence, and compliance issues to stakeholders, including senior executives, regulators, employees, and clients. Program Structure The 4-year Bachelor\u2019s Degree program contains 156 credits combining from 106 credits of coursework, 48 credits of internship and 2 credits of Industrial Placement Report. The courses are divided into three categories, including Common Courses, Specialized Courses, and Elective Courses. Common courses PRO101: Computer Fundamentals HUM101: Introduction to Humanities KHM101: Introduction to Khmer Studies and History RES101: Research Methods SDE101: Social and Digital Entrepreneurship ENG103: Academic Writing Skills PHI101: Philosophy and Anthropology of Technology Internship 9 internships (3 internships per term) Specialised courses RMB101: Principles of Economics RMB102: Introduction to Risk Management RMB103: Introduction to Business Intelligence RMB104: Introduction to Financial Accounting RMB105: Statistics and Probability RMB106: Introduction to Risk Assessment RMB107: Introduction to Financial Management RMB208: Risk Assessment and Modelling RMB209: Data Analytics and Visualization RMB210: Business Ethics and Values RMB211: Cybersecurity in Risk Management RMB212: Fraud Detection and Prevention RMB213: Information Security and Privacy RMB214: Project Management RMB215: Managerial Accounting RMB216: Data Warehousing in Business RMB217: Corporate Social Responsibility and Sustainability RMB218: Risk Assessment and Business Analytics RMB319: Enterprise Risk Management RMB320: Risk-based Decision Making RMB321: Credit Risk Management RMB322: Strategic Business Planning RMB323: Reputational Risk Management RMB324: Digital Marketing Analytics RMB325: Operational Risk Management RMB326: Risk-based Internal Auditing and Compliance RMB327: Data Mining and Predictive Analytics RMB328: Advanced Risk Management Strategies RMB329: Capital Budgeting and Investment Analysis IND330: Industry Orientation Elective courses ENV101: Environment and Geography ENG101: Core English 01 CHN101: Chinese 01 GLO101: Global Studies LIT101: Literature Studies ENG101: Core English 02 CHN101: Chinese 02 Job Prospects Risk Management Analyst\/ Consultant Business Intelligence Analyst\/ Consultant Financial Analyst\/ Consultant Market Trend Analyst\/ Consultant Compliance, Information Security and Data Analyst Risk Management and Business Intelligence Strategist<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":7,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-32012","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry","post-no-thumbnail"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/32012","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/7"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=32012"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/32012\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":37610,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/32012\/revisions\/37610"}],"wp:at